#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
server.py — the Study Room's one-command localhost server (Plan 22-02).

`python3 server.py` serves the whole app at http://127.0.0.1:8747 — static
files (index.html, tokens.css, app.js, vendor/) plus a small JSON API over
the tested study_lib engine. Fully offline; stdlib only (D-01).

Routes:
  GET  /                 index.html (static, directory pinned to the repo root)
  GET  /api/status       {ok, items, library_root, store_exists, survey_url?}
  GET  /api/items        the FULL store object (schema_version + meta + items)
  GET  /lib/<id>         an item's snapshot bytes, resolved by id LOOKUP in
                         the store — never from the URL path (no traversal)
  GET  /lib/<id>/att/<basename>
                         one of a note's attached pictures (22-uat) —
                         served STRICTLY by store lookup: the id must exist
                         and the %-decoded basename must be an exact member
                         of the item's attachments list; anything else 404s
  GET  /api/layout       {ok, layout} — the stored room arrangement, or
                         null when layout.json is missing or unreadable
                         (fail-OPEN read: the room keeps its shipped
                         positions; layout.json sits BESIDE items.json,
                         never inside it — D-04)
  GET  /api/import-progress
                         the import job's snapshot (25-03): {ok, state,
                         total, done, started_ms, report, message} — the
                         import screen re-reads it with a chained one-shot
                         re-arm; the worker finishes server-side whether
                         or not anyone is watching
  GET  /api/librarian/status
                         {ok, available, why, auth, enabled, version_ok} —
                         the librarian seam's fail-open answer (26-01,
                         SRM-11): a tier holding a fill that can actually
                         answer + the librarian_enabled meta flag
                         (26.93-07/08 — no program on PATH is consulted).
                         Unavailable is ALWAYS
                         a 200 with plain words — the room shows no error
                         states, and with the flag off it is byte-identical
                         to the no-AI build
  GET  /api/librarian/progress
                         the pre-sort job's snapshot (26-02): state /
                         total / done / usage / auth / message /
                         unknown_id_verdicts, plus the notebook's shelf
                         — 26.93-06: `usage` carries the provider's OWN
                         token counts, per provider; no dollar figure is
                         computed anywhere, and how spend is shown is map
                         ticket #34's, open and downstream. `cost_usd` is
                         still on the dict, frozen at 0.0, until 26.93-11
                         removes the client render that reads it
                         counts and the verdicts map itself — the client
                         joins verdicts to items through the GATED core
                         selector, so a hand-edited suggestions.json
                         still cannot render a fenced item
  POST /api/library      {path} — pick/confirm the library folder (D-07)
  POST /api/scan         {path} — dry-run: adapter-aware counts only,
                         nothing copied (25-03: study_lib.scan_source owns
                         the walk — adapter name + conversation counts for
                         export sources ride the established fields)
  POST /api/import       {path, consolidation} — import into the library;
                         path + consolidation shape are validated
                         fail-closed BEFORE anything else — a malformed
                         request 400s, imports nothing, and spawns no
                         worker (RV-2). An accepted import runs in a
                         server-side worker thread holding WRITE_LOCK;
                         the POST answers immediately with {ok, running,
                         total}; a second import while one runs is
                         refused 400 in plain words (25-03)
  POST /api/state        {changes: [{id, to, via, ...}]} — validated batch;
                         side-fields last_opened_ms / resting_until_ms /
                         trigger (D-08 hidden overlay) ride each change
  POST /api/meta         whitelisted-key shallow merge into store meta; the
                         Phase 23 keys (filters, cover_offers, current_cover,
                         incidents) are shape-validated fail-closed, and
                         `incidents` is append-only: the server stamps `at`
                         itself and caps the list at the newest INCIDENT_CAP.
                         The Phase 24 H10 room counters (room_entries,
                         object_opens) are fail-closed validated too (D-17),
                         and so is the consolidation tri-state — exactly
                         true, false, or null (D-11/D-14, RV-2). The Phase
                         26 librarian_enabled flag is a bool exactly
                         (26-01, SRM-11) — absent = off = the no-AI room
  POST /api/layout       whole-document replace of layout.json (Phase 24.1,
                         D-03/D-04/D-05): validate_layout runs fail-closed
                         BEFORE the lock — version pin, known object ids
                         only, in-bounds 12px-grid positions, an
                         accessory-sprite name roster (never a path), and
                         the four functional objects may never appear in
                         `removed` (the move-only law). A bad shape 400s
                         and nothing is written; an accepted document is
                         written atomically on drop
  POST /api/librarian/presort
                         {consent: bool} — start one pre-sort run (26-02,
                         pull-only: the run begins at the user's tap and
                         nowhere else). consent is per-run and never
                         sticky; fail-closed validation before anything
                         spawns; unavailable answers 200 {available:
                         false} with zero work; one run at a time. The
                         worker writes librarian/suggestions.json ONLY —
                         never the store
  POST /api/librarian/presort/stop
                         {} — end a running pre-sort at its next batch
                         boundary (26.99955 UAT G-…-05). Cooperative,
                         never a thread kill: the worker checks a flag
                         between batches, so everything already verdicted
                         stays verdicted and starting again carries on
                         from there. Nothing running answers as calmly as
                         something running
  POST /api/librarian/ack
                         {id, user_took} — stamp what the user did with a
                         suggestion (blessed | never_show | skipped) into
                         the notebook file; the id must already hold a
                         verdict; item state itself changes only through
                         /api/state, from the user's own tap (law 2/7)
  GET  /api/librarian/notes
                         reveal-only (26-03, SRM-12): list the gift files
                         under librarian/notes/ as [{name, kind, unread}],
                         or hand one back verbatim with ?read=<name>.
                         PURE file reads — zero subprocess, zero store
                         access: the desk-open path calls this, and
                         desk-open must stay instant and offline. Missing
                         dir or files = empty memory, never an error
  POST /api/librarian/note
                         {} — the explicit ask (26-03): one user tap asks
                         the librarian to write the desk note, drawn from
                         blessed material ONLY (scope="note"), post-checked
                         server-side before any file is written. The other
                         doorway is the pre-sort run's final step when the
                         POSTed {note: true} asked for it — generation
                         exists nowhere else (pull-only, law 1)
  POST /api/librarian/read
                         {name} — stamp one gift file read into
                         librarian/read.json (the notebook record half of
                         "reading marks read"); the file itself is never
                         touched or deleted
  POST /api/librarian/dismiss
                         {topic} — permanent dismissal (T-26-14): appends
                         {topic, at} to librarian/dismissed.json and the
                         server hard-filters against it — the AI never gets
                         to overrule the file. 26.995-06 (D-05): on the
                         reflection path that filter is now a WHOLE-DRAFT
                         rejection, because the question slot it used to
                         empty no longer exists
  POST /api/librarian/not-relevant
                         {id} — `not relevant` (26.95-31, D-13/D-14): appends
                         {item_id, origin_path, at} to
                         librarian/not-relevant.json, and that record
                         withdraws the item from every librarian PROPOSAL
                         surface, permanently and across cycles. A match on
                         EITHER key counts (owner ruling, 2026-08-15).
                         Fail-closed on an id the store does not hold or the
                         fence excludes — ONE sentence for both, so an error
                         can never answer "is there a never-show item here?".
                         It changes no item state whatever: the picture stays
                         unseen, stays in Manage, stays findable, and no
                         sixth state is created. The reversal is that the
                         file is hers to open and delete
  GET  /api/librarian/memory
                         the librarian's two memories (26.95-31, SRM-13):
                         {not_relevant_ids, last_offer_ms} — ids and ONE
                         integer, every id screened through the fence, and no
                         content of any kind. Pure fail-open reads: an
                         unreadable file or a store that will not load is an
                         empty memory and a null stamp, never an error
  GET  /api/librarian/what-it-knows
                         what SHE is shown (26.995-13, C-3/C-7, SRM-13):
                         {memory} — the SHIPPED derived block in her ranked
                         order, or null, which is her empty state. ⛔ NOT the
                         route above: that one is the OFFER memory and carries
                         no content by design, and her own sentences are
                         content. The derivation is CALLED, so the read-time
                         fence screen is the same one, never a second. The
                         room's essay BODIES and every stamp are dropped here
  POST /api/librarian/what-it-knows/strike
                         {text} — she takes one of her own sentences back
                         (26.995-13, D-21). A REAL deletion from
                         librarian/your-sentences.json, matched by exact text;
                         fail-closed on a blank or wrong-shaped ask, {ok} when
                         it matches nothing. ⛔ Only HER sentences are
                         strikeable — the kept-and-passed half is derived from
                         the ledger, so a strike there would be undone by the
                         next derivation and would damage the
                         never-repeat-a-name check
  POST /api/librarian/session
                         {consent: bool, intent?} — start one reflection
                         session (26.7-02, D-32/D-33): the presort
                         worker's sibling. Fail-closed consent check,
                         availability gate, one job at a time; the pool
                         is built ONLY by build_librarian_payload(store,
                         "reflection",
                         session_marker=meta.last_reflection_ms); an
                         empty pool answers {nothing_new: true, held} and
                         runs ZERO generation (D-10). The worker writes
                         librarian/session.json ONLY — never the store,
                         and never the marker (D-11: stamped at session
                         COMPLETION — the close route). 26.7-05 (D-03):
                         intent "resume" re-opens the one spent offer
                         (state offered → active) and answers the stored
                         {pool, draft, chat} whole (26.995-06 D-05:
                         no question field; 26.995-12 D-13: no coda
                         field);
                         intent "discard" lets the held draft go, then
                         proceeds with the normal fresh beat; a fresh
                         beat that finds an unanswered spent offer
                         (state "offered") discards it silently and
                         proceeds — one offer per held draft, ever
  GET  /api/librarian/session
                         the session file's readout (26.7-02): {state,
                         draft, name, consented, chat} —
                         fail-open, an absent file answers {state:
                         "none"}; a pure file read, zero store access.
                         26.7-05 (D-03): ?beat=start is the candle tap's
                         session-start read — a resumable file (state
                         active/held) transitions to "offered" and
                         persists ATOMICALLY BEFORE the answer carries
                         offer:true (the write IS the one offer being
                         spent — a crash mid-offer can never re-ask)
  POST /api/librarian/refine
                         {text} — ONE chat-refine turn (26.7-03, D-01/
                         D-04/D-07, AI-SPEC §4 decision of record):
                         stateless full-context re-send. The per-turn doc
                         {pool, draft, chat[-CHAT_TURN_CAP:]} is rebuilt
                         from librarian/session.json ALONE — the pool
                         re-sent byte-identical, never recomputed — and
                         makes ONE run through the choke point. Refused
                         in plain words when no active session with a
                         recorded consent answer waits (the D-04 per-turn
                         check); busy-gated like every librarian job. On
                         success the user turn, the librarian's reply,
                         and the revised draft persist TOGETHER in one
                         atomic session.json rewrite; on ANY failure the
                         file is byte-untouched — the same turn is
                         re-sendable and no duplicate ever persists
  POST /api/librarian/session/close
                         {outcome: "save"|"pass"} — the three-path gate's
                         terminal verbs (26.7-04, D-28/D-11/D-16): her
                         save — and only her save — materializes the
                         essay as a NEW store item (source
                         "librarian"), injects the {id, kind:
                         "reflection"} proposal, and promotes it through
                         the shipped consent verb — inject + promote
                         under ONE _INSIGHTS_LOCK hold, so the
                         deterministic insights refresh can never wipe
                         it. Both outcomes stamp last_reflection_ms (the
                         ONLY writer of the D-11 marker — session
                         COMPLETION, nothing else) and discard
                         librarian/session.json. A close with no active
                         session is a refused no-op (no double stamp, no
                         duplicate book). With the default-OFF
                         reflection_writeback_enabled toggle exactly
                         True, a save ALSO writes ONE NEW .md into the
                         vault's Claude's observation/Journal analysis/
                         AFTER every lock releases (D-06) — a write-back
                         failure is a counted quiet fact on the answer,
                         never a lost book
  POST /api/librarian/reach-date
                         {seed_id} — the front call's own round trip
                         (26.95-33, P-7), taken BEFORE any candidate is
                         computed and ONLY when the Seed's own file knows no
                         date. Answers {ok, fortnight, from}: one integer
                         and one token, never an id, so this route can
                         neither order nor pick a result. Every way the call
                         can fail — declined, any closed-set failure token,
                         a tier with no fill this job may use, an answer cut
                         off, a window that does not parse — lands on
                         today's calendar fortnight, silently; and the year
                         bound is no longer here at all (D-05 amendment,
                         2026-08-16); nothing is written anywhere

Safety posture:
  - binds 127.0.0.1 explicitly; never all interfaces
  - Host-header allowlist (localhost / 127.0.0.1) on /api/ and /lib/ routes —
    a cheap DNS-rebinding guard; no CORS headers are ever emitted
  - every items.json read-modify-write happens inside WRITE_LOCK
    (ThreadingHTTPServer runs handlers concurrently)
  - a corrupt items.json means REFUSE (StoreCorruptError) — the server never
    writes a fresh store over user judgments
  - a schema-v1 items.json is migrated to v2 exactly once, at startup (and on
    an /api/library re-point), under WRITE_LOCK, AFTER a one-time
    items.json.v1.bak backup; unknown or newer versions refuse, never rewrite
  - POST bodies are capped at 1 MB (413 beyond)
  - importing this module binds no socket: use create_server(...) or main()
"""
