# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 26.87-04 (D-01/D-21, SE-1/SE-2): the config-ask key families. TWO tuples,
# not one, because "what the CHAT may reach" and "what the MODEL may NAME at
# all" are different questions with different blast radii.
#
# CONFIGURABLE_KEYS is the only set the CHAT may reach. Manage still exposes
# exactly what it exposes today: this bounds the chat, not the panes.
#
# What is EXCLUDED, and why the exclusion IS the fence:
#   * pure machinery — cycle, current_shelf, incidents, room_entries,
#     object_opens, last_entry_ms, cover_offers, current_cover. Nobody asks
#     for these in words, and a sentence that could move them could corrupt
#     the reading loop.
#   * silent law-3 stamps — last_visit_ms, last_reflection_ms. Their own
#     docstrings say they are NEVER rendered; a chat that could set them
#     could re-open the time gap law 3 exists to close.
#   * setup latches — habit_anchor, habit_anchor_asked, onboarding_complete.
#     The first TWO have NO validator at all and land in meta verbatim
#     through handle_meta's shallow merge, which is exactly why D-02's "each
#     addition still passes an existing validator" was FALSE for them
#     (SE-2). Until they have one, the chat may not name them.
#
# librarian_name, filters, fenced_roster and connected_sources are
# SERVER-RESOLVED value classes, handled in 26.87-07: the chat may reach
# them, but the MODEL may never carry their values — fenced_roster's current
# value IS her declared-sensitive folder list and filters values are
# item-derived (SE-1).
#
# 26.87-09 ADDED `voice_model` BY NAME to BOTH tuples below (appended to
# CONFIGURABLE_KEYS, a seventh literal in MODEL_PROPOSABLE_KEYS) and inserted
# it into META_KEYS ABOVE that tuple's closing member, because a shipped
# test pins connected_sources as the last entry. It is the ONE closed-STRING
# member of the proposable set: its value class is a THREE-MEMBER PUBLIC
# CONSTANT (VOICE_MODELS), which is exactly why it may cross the ask seam
# where filters (item-derived) and fenced_roster (her declared-sensitive
# folder list) may not.
#
# 26.95-34 ADDS `blessing_batch_size` BY NAME to BOTH tuples below (appended
# to CONFIGURABLE_KEYS, an eighth literal in MODEL_PROPOSABLE_KEYS) and
# inserts it into META_KEYS above that tuple's closing member, for the same
# shipped-test reason. It is the ONE BOUNDED-INTEGER member of the proposable
# set: its value class is a whole number between two module constants, which
# is a public, bounded, non-item-derived class in exactly the way voice_model's
# is — and unlike filters or fenced_roster, whose values ARE her library and
# her declared-sensitive folders.
