# whole dollar. 26.99-14 made the figure real CENTS by her ruling, and at the
# UAT she chose the `$` notation for them — so the ending would have read
# "$0.30 dollar.", which is NOT what she approved. That trailing word is the
# only thing that came off. ⛔ It was deleted programmatically out of the
# bytes already in this file rather than retyped, and ⛔ nothing else in her
# sentence moved: not a capital, not a comma, not the grammar a later reader
# might take for an error.
#
# ⚠⚠ AND SHE CHOSE WHERE THE SYMBOL LIVES. Asked at a blocking checkpoint on
# 26.99-15 — in her sentence, or on the number the room fills in — she
# answered, verbatim: "On the number". ⛔ So there is STILL no currency symbol
# anywhere in this constant, because she did not write one. The `$` is
# composed onto the FIGURE in `forecast_line` and reaches her screen through
# the substitution, and her sentence gained no new character at all.
#
# ⚠ THE AUTHORISATION TO TOUCH HER SENTENCE AT ALL IS TWO INSTRUMENTS AND
# ONLY TWO: her G-7 ruling at the UAT, plus her checkpoint answer on
# 26.99-15. ⛔ It is spent. A later reader who wants this line different needs
# HER — D-14 rations a pass over her words to one, and a second pass is a
# second thing to ask her for, not a reading of this comment.
#
# ⚠ THE SLOT IS STILL HERS AND IS STILL ASSERTED AT EXACTLY ONE, re-derived
# below over the new bytes and ⛔ never relaxed to fit them.
FORECAST_MSG = "This task may consume a good amount power for librarian's brain, the estimate will be x."  # noqa: E501

# ⚠ A COUNT, ASSERTED AT IMPORT — the FAILURE_SENTENCES discipline one
# screen up. Her sentence carries exactly ONE standalone slot. A second
# would make the render ambiguous and a zeroth would make it silently
# figure-less; both are programming errors rather than things that can
# happen at run time, which is why this is an assertion and not a test.
_FORECAST_SLOT = re.compile(r"(?<![A-Za-z0-9])x(?![A-Za-z0-9])")
assert len(_FORECAST_SLOT.findall(FORECAST_MSG)) == 1, (
    "the owner's forecast sentence must carry exactly one slot; found "
    + repr(_FORECAST_SLOT.findall(FORECAST_MSG)))


def forecast_line(job, calls, routing):
    """Her sentence with the figure in its slot, or None.

    ⛔ SILENCE RENDERS NOTHING AT ALL — not an empty state, not a line
    saying the room does not know. Absence, the way `renderCleaningRuns`
    treats nothing-to-take-back: a slot with no words renders nothing.

    ⚠⚠ THE FIGURE IS COMPOSED FROM INTEGER ARITHMETIC AND NOTHING ELSE
    (26.99-15, G-7). `forecast_usd` answers whole CENTS as an `int`; the
    dollars and the two places below are integer division and modulo on that
    count. ⛔ NEVER `%.2f` OVER A FLOAT, and never a float anywhere near
    this — a float is exactly how `0.30` becomes `0.3` or
    `0.30000000000004`, on the one number in the room that exists to be
    conservative and to be trusted. ⛔ Two decimal places always: `0.3` or
    `1` is not the shape she approved.

    ⚠⚠ THE `$` IS PUT ON THE FIGURE, NOT INTO HER WORDS, and that was her
    answer at a blocking checkpoint on 26.99-15 — verbatim, "On the number".
    So the symbol is composed here and arrives through the substitution;
    `FORECAST_MSG` carries none.

    ⚠ The composed string is digits, one `$` and one `.` — no backslash, so
    it passes through `re.sub`'s replacement template untouched.

    ⚠ ONE CONSTANT, ONE READER. The finished sentence crosses the wire, so
    the client holds no literal of her words and the two surfaces cannot
    drift apart. Pure."""
    figure = forecast_usd(job, calls, routing)
    if figure is None:
        return None
    shown = "$%d.%02d" % (figure // 100, figure % 100)
    return _FORECAST_SLOT.sub(shown, FORECAST_MSG, count=1)


def forecast_block():
    """The room's ONE money field, for `handle_librarian_status`.

    ⚠ IT RIDES THE STATUS READ rather than taking a route of its own, for
    the reason the consent block does: that read already happens on exactly
    the occasions the sentence is needed — `startReflectionSession` fetches
    it before a sitting's consent card can paint — and a second route would
    be a second surface to keep honest.

    ⚠ AND IT IS CHEAP BY CONSTRUCTION. The reflection's call count is a
    measured coefficient rather than a batch count, so this costs one dict
    read and one routing resolve, and never a payload build, on a route the
    room calls on every open.

    ⛔ NOTHING HERE IS STORED. The figure is computed, rendered into her
    sentence, and forgotten. ⚠ Fail-open like every other field on this
    route: a resolve that raises answers SILENCE, never an error state, and
    never a zero."""
    try:
        return {"forecast_line": forecast_line(
            "reflection", LIBRARIAN_REFLECTION_CALLS_PER_SITTING,
            resolve_librarian_routing())}
    except Exception:
        return {"forecast_line": None}


def failure_sentence(token, provider=None):
    """One failure token as plain words — the ONE reader of FAILURE_SENTENCES.

    Every surface goes through here rather than indexing the map itself, so
    the `{provider}` fill happens in exactly one place and an unknown token
    can never reach her as a blank line or a raw machine word. A token
    outside the closed register is a programming error rather than something
    that can happen at run time (the set equality above), so the fallback is
    deliberately the plainest true sentence already in the map rather than a
    new one nobody reviewed.

    Pure: no store read, no file, no clock."""
    sentence = FAILURE_SENTENCES.get(token) or FAILURE_SENTENCES["malformed"]
    who = provider or "the librarian's provider"
    return sentence.replace("{provider}", who)


