#
# The librarian's older route from store bytes to a model stood on these lines:
# a spawned command line, fed on standard input, with a version floor and an
# installed-program look-up in front of it. It is gone. Everything the
# librarian asks now goes through ONE function — `call_librarian` in
# `librarian_call` — so the fence's central claim stopped being an argument
# about which of two routes happens to be wired and became a count: there is
# one, and a static gate can say so.
#
# ⚠ ONE spawned-program call site survives in this file, further down, and it
# belongs to the vault tidy-up. That is deliberate, and it is a DIFFERENT TRUST
# TIER on purpose: the librarian's path is hermetic and may read only what the
# fence builder hands it, while the vault path runs the owner's own skill over
# her own files with tools and permissions deliberately on. Two paths with two
# postures is the design; one path pretending to be both is the thing this
# deletion makes impossible.
#
# What was LOST, said plainly rather than left for a reader to discover: the
# strongest evidence this project had about the librarian's inputs used to be a
# recorded command line, read back after the fact. The replacement reads the
# same facts out of a recorded request body, which proves what the app sends —
# not what the provider does with it afterward (#24).
#
# A later reader who finds an empty space wonders. This is the sentence.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


def _envelope_model(envelope):
    """The alias the envelope REPORTED, or None — the D-28.2 model record.

    THE KEY PATH IS MEASURED, NOT GUESSED (26.87-03, the owner-approved
    real-CLI dry run): there is NO top-level `model` key. The path is
    `modelUsage`, a dict KEYED BY THE MODEL ID, whose value carries the
    stable `canonicalModel` alias beside the usage numbers:

        envelope["modelUsage"] -> {"<dated id>": {..., "canonicalModel": ...}}

    FAILS OPEN TO A NULL RECORD, three ways, because `modelUsage` can be
    absent or empty on an error envelope and its key set is NOT guaranteed
    to be size 1: a missing or non-dict map answers None; a map with
    anything other than exactly ONE entry answers None (picking one of
    several would be a guess wearing a fact's clothes); and an entry with no
    usable canonicalModel falls back to the dated key itself, then to None.
    Never indexes blindly, never raises. Pure."""
    usage = envelope.get("modelUsage") if isinstance(envelope, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(usage, dict) or len(usage) != 1:
        return None
    key = next(iter(usage))
    row = usage[key]
    if isinstance(row, dict):
        alias = row.get("canonicalModel")
        if isinstance(alias, str) and alias.strip():
            return alias.strip()
    return key.strip() if isinstance(key, str) and key.strip() else None


