#
# ⛔⛔ HER RULING, 2026-08-21, VERBATIM: "The model judges each one"
# (26.995-COPY.md § C-4 continuation beat 3). She was asked a second time
# because two things inside her 2026-08-18 answer had never been put to her as
# one question, and because a cost had never been named: judging is a new job,
# so it is a permanent new row on the standing per-job list, and the room will
# not start until two more sentences of hers exist for it. She held her answer
# with both costs on the table.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND HER DEFINITION OF THE RULE, RULED IN THE SAME SITTING (beat 2, the
# WIDE reading, verbatim): "Any ending that points you toward doing something
# is out, gentle or not." She was shown the repo's own canonical good essay —
# it ended "Use: cast on the small swatch tonight and let it be enough." — and
# told that under the wide reading that essay is thrown away and rewritten.
# She chose it anyway, and the fixture was rewritten.
#
# ⛔ WHY THIS IS A MODEL CALL AND NOT A PATTERN. 26.995-03 task 4 built the
# best honest non-model mechanism, scored it, and HALTED: 8/8 on the fixtures
# it was fitted to and 3/5 held out, wrong in BOTH directions. Its decisive
# failure was that it rejected "let that be enough." — a legal form, and
# literally the second half of its own reject fixture. The legal ending and
# the illegal one differ by INTENT, not by structure, and no list of words
# separates them. ⛔ A later plan may not quietly revive one: it would pass
# those same eight fixtures and be pinned as correct.
#
# ⬜⬜ THE PROMPT BELOW IS AN AGENT'S READING OF HER RULING, NOT HER WORDS,
# and it is marked here for exactly the reason 26.995-19's offline rubric line
# is marked (owed item W-2): it is the place her rule is turned into something
